-- title:
--   Idelic presentation of the class group of a Dedekind domain
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a Dedekind domain with field of fractions $K$, so that $K$ is an $R$-algebra realising $K$ as the fraction field of $R$, and let $\mathbb{A}$ denote the finite adele ring `FiniteAdeleRing R K` of $R$ relative to $K$, i.e. the restricted product of the completions $K_v$ of $K$ at the primes $v$ in the height-one spectrum of $R$ with respect to the valuation rings $\mathcal{O}_v$. Inside $\mathbb{A}^\times$ consider two subgroups: first `unitIdeles R K`, whose elements are the units $\delta$ of $\mathbb{A}$ such that for every height-one prime $v$ of $R$ the component $\delta_v$ lies in $\mathcal{O}_v$ and likewise every component of $\delta^{-1}$ lies in $\mathcal{O}_v$; and second the image of $K^\times$ under the map of unit groups induced by the structure morphism $K \to \mathbb{A}$, that is, the group of principal ideles. The theorem asserts that the type of group isomorphisms between the ideal class group $\mathrm{ClassGroup}\ R$ and the quotient of $\mathbb{A}^\times$ by the subgroup generated by these two subgroups (their join, which since $\mathbb{A}^\times$ is commutative is just their product) is nonempty: some such isomorphism exists. No particular isomorphism is named, and no finiteness of the class group or number-field hypothesis is assumed.
--
--   This is the idelic description of the class group, $\mathrm{Cl}(R) \cong \mathbb{A}^\times/(\widehat{R}^\times K^\times)$, classically obtained from the content map $\delta \mapsto [\prod_v \mathfrak{p}_v^{\mathrm{ord}_v \delta_v}]$; here only the existence of an isomorphism of groups is recorded. It is used in the computation of the index of the product of the principal ideles with the group of ideles that are units outside a finite set, which for a number field is expressed through the class number.
-- source:
